row.cell:
From the Minister in China (tel.)
Report of capture of Sheklung by
                            Chen Chiung-ming, November 12, and retreat of Sun’s forces into Canton;
                            presence of U. S. S. Asheville at Canton;
                            arrangement for protection of Americans.

To the British Chargé
General
                            concurrence in principles set forth in British memorandum of June 30;
                            doubt, however, that demands could be secured by naval demonstration;
                            and suggestion that withdrawal of recognition might prove effective as
                            means of exerting pressure.
